    "body": "I believe that specifically for the close case (which supplies afterAllUnloads), we delay destroying until all descendants have had a chance to fire their unload events.\r\n\r\nIn other destroy cases, e.g. force-closing, we do not delay. But those don't call \"unload a document and all its descendants\"; they go straight to \"destroy a top-level traversable\".",
